From 6daea0b0076f6e60df8916732cdd7ec17f161e65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:59:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): [daveey] sidebar paints from a boot snapshot
 before the backend is up

Cold start showed a blank window for ~7.7 s: the full-screen CONNECTING
overlay waits for the local backend (~6 s to boot), and every sidebar row
(hub-sync replica rows, the projects tree) is served by that backend.

- electron/sidebar-boot-snapshot.ts: Electron main reads hub.db read-only
  (a port of hub-sync hubview.py sessions(): published + replica rows,
  pending requests, primary-mode shared-field overlay, activity order) and
  the last projects tree (userData/sidebar-boot-snapshot.json). The first
  window reads both over sync IPC (hermes:boot-snapshot:read).
- src/store/boot-snapshot.ts: seeds the sidebar fallback inputs with every
  gateway's rows, this one's included, and the projects tree while empty.
  Live lists replace them per owner (mergeOfflineFallback freshness). The
  live tree is saved (debounced, no running state) for the next launch.
- The CONNECTING overlay stays down on a cold boot whose sidebar painted from
  the snapshot (same as a post-boot reconnect).
- hub-sync plugin: a failed replica read publishes nothing, so it never
  wipes rows already showing.
- [sidebar-timing] log line: ms from process start to first sidebar rows and
  to the first live list, and the rows' source.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
